    "title": "AI Firms Are Buying Old Books in Bulk, Then Shredding Them",
    "source_text": "AI Firms Are Buying Old Books in Bulk — Then Shredding Them.\nA July 2026 investigation found brokers marketing bulk physical book acquisition to AI developers, offering 1,000 to 1 million titles per order with buyer anonymity and NDAs attached. Pre-2022 print sells at a premium because it's guaranteed human-written, and destructive scanning is chosen for cost rather than necessity — non-destructive robots exist, but cutting spines is cheaper at scale. No public reporting has yet tied a specific completed order to a named AI buyer.",
