        "research": {
            "topic": "AI firms bulk-buying and destroying print books for training data",
            "summary": "Broker ISBNdb is openly selling bulk pre-2022 print books to anonymous AI labs at 1,000–1,000,000 units per order under strict NDAs, pitched as the last text corpus guaranteed free of AI slop. The practice is already documented at Anthropic, whose 'Project Panama' bought, spine-cut, scanned and pulped millions of used books — ruled fair use by Judge Alsup in June 2025.",
